From: knulli
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: tolerate a system with no DRM subsystem

The fbdev Mali boards have no /sys/class/drm, and the throwing
directory_iterator overload aborts the process before the HUD ever
starts.  Use the error_code overload: on failure the iterator compares
equal to end() and we simply find no GPUs, which the rest of the class
already handles.

--- a/src/gpu.cpp
+++ b/src/gpu.cpp
@@ -8,7 +8,13 @@
     std::set<std::string> gpu_entries;
     auto params = early_params ? early_params : get_params().get();
 
-    for (const auto& entry : fs::directory_iterator("/sys/class/drm")) {
+    std::error_code drm_ec;
+    fs::directory_iterator drm_nodes("/sys/class/drm", drm_ec);
+    if (drm_ec)
+        SPDLOG_WARN("Cannot read /sys/class/drm ({}), no GPU metrics will be shown",
+                    drm_ec.message());
+
+    for (const auto& entry : drm_nodes) {
         if (!entry.is_directory())
             continue;
 
